note: batch 11b (R70.2-1): the derive helper attribute `#[named(…)]` of the derive `depot::Named` moves across `#[derive(Debug)]`: the compiler keeps the helper on the item, so it is no attribute macro, and the fact has no spotlight (a limit of 10n2: the name list took it as an attribute macro)
rule-: R70.2-1
must_not_match: an attribute macro moves across a derive
=== both Cargo.toml
[workspace]
members = ["shop", "depot"]
resolver = "2"
=== both depot/Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "depot"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"

[lib]
proc-macro = true
=== both depot/src/lib.rs
use proc_macro::TokenStream;

#[proc_macro_derive(Named, attributes(named))]
pub fn named(_item: TokenStream) -> TokenStream {
    TokenStream::new()
}
=== both shop/Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "shop"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"

[dependencies]
depot = { path = "../depot" }
=== old shop/src/lib.rs
#[derive(depot::Named)]
#[named(rename = "x")]
#[derive(Debug)]
pub struct Item {
    pub a: u8,
}
=== new shop/src/lib.rs
#[derive(depot::Named)]
#[derive(Debug)]
#[named(rename = "x")]
pub struct Item {
    pub a: u8,
}
